/-!
# Actual integral homology and cohomology of Euclidean spheres

The standard sphere is the literal unit sphere in real Euclidean space.
Latitude coordinates construct its suspension homeomorphism; the genuine
two-cone cover then gives the original singular Mayer--Vietoris maps.
The native circle computation starts the induction. Every positive
dimensional sphere has infinite cyclic groups in degrees zero and its
dimension, and zero groups in all other degrees. All homology groups are
free and finitely generated. The cohomology marking is the genuine
evaluation dual, with an actual top pairing equal to one.

These results concern the standard spheres themselves. They neither
identify the constructed threefold with a sphere nor assume a sphere
recognition, smooth classification, or orientation-comparison theorem.
-/
